@@ -0,0 +1,195 @@
+Additional workarounds for stdexec with nvcc 12.8 and a GCC 13 host compiler.
+
+The original nvcc workarounds allow parsing HPX's execution headers, but sender
+instantiations still fail in nvcc's generated host code. This incremental patch
+addresses callable non-type template parameters, unintended cv/ref qualifiers,
+virtual diagnostic types, GCC copy elision, and references to constexpr global
+function objects from host/device functions. A dependent sync_wait alias is
+spelled through a helper to preserve its result type in generated host code.
+
+Use STDEXEC_DEMANGLE_SENDER_NAMES consistently in HPX and its consumers; it
+selects a different sender representation. HPX's Stdexec interface target
+exports this definition for nvcc builds. These workarounds enable host-side
+sender machinery in CUDA translation units, not arbitrary GPU sender execution.
+
+Keep this patch separate so existing FetchContent checkouts with the earlier
+nvcc patches can acquire it. It applies to stdexec commit
+04de75de5807e73a229acf047c6976575e313359, pinned by HPX 2.0.0-rc1.
+
